 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** $O(M)$ for projection of $M$ Gaussians, plus $O(M \log M)$ for sorting by depth. Rasterization is proportional to the number of pixels covered by splats.
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(M)$ to store projected Gaussian attributes.
+- **Time Complexity:** Not given in the sources.
+- **Memory Complexity:** Not given in the sources.
 - **Performance:** Enables real-time rendering of millions of Gaussians (e.g., 134 fps on Mip-NeRF360) by avoiding ray marching [S3].
-- **Strengths:** Closed-form projection allows differentiability and fast GPU/CPU rasterization. The local affine approximation is accurate for small splats [S3].
-- **Limitations:** The linearization error increases for large splats or extreme perspective, potentially causing geometric inaccuracies [S3]. Singularities are handled by stabilization but may introduce slight blurring if $\epsilon_{2d}$ is too large [S2].
